From 84540a577c12535d1109f14e58bca4fc2db4b2ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/46] GDN: read the qwen35 SSM state from the cache by ids;
 Vulkan writes the rollback snapshots straight into the cache

Port of the GLM series patch 0009 to qwen35 / qwen35moe (MTP rollback snapshots, n_rs_seq > 0):
- ggml_gated_delta_net_ids(q, k, v, g, beta, states, ids, K): the initial state of seq s is row ids[s] of states
  (src[6]). CPU reference; Vulkan binds ids; other backends report it unsupported.
- qwen35 / qwen35moe: one seq, one cell, no state to clear, snapshots kept and a device that supports the op: read
  the SSM state straight from its cache row through s_copy instead of the 3 MiB build_rs gather per layer
  (env LLAMA_GDN_NO_STATE_IDS=1 turns it off).
- Vulkan: fuse GATED_DELTA_NET -> views -> CPY of its snapshots into the recurrent cache (GDN_CACHE): the shader
  writes the snapshots to the cache rows directly and the CPY is skipped. graph_optimize keeps GDN + views + CPY
  adjacent and moves independent nodes in between (qwen35 layer 0: the z gate) behind the CPY.
- Unused ids binding gets the (read-only) state buffer: binding the written dst there made n_seqs = 2 tests flaky.
- test-backend-ops: GATED_DELTA_NET_IDS_CACHE (cache layout with K rollback planes, ids into each plane, in-place
  snapshot write), plus qwen35 shapes (48 heads of 128, scalar gate, K = 5).

Qwen3.8-27B UD-IQ4_XS MTP n4 verify (5 tokens), perf logger: GDN snapshot CPY 3.2 -> 0.8 ms (the rest are conv-state
copies), state GET_ROWS 1.1 -> 0.2 ms, and the matvecs after the GDN no longer pay the snapshot writeback:
5120x6144 (ssm_out / attn_output) at n=5 157 -> 100 us (iq4_xs), 179 -> 133 (q5_K), 166 -> 104 (q4_K).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
